          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:28:02Z",
          "note": "mrRefreshDirtyDots() is a documented no-op stub. During inline editing, dirty dots are only updated on full re-renders (triggered by Done/Cancel/action buttons), not on every keystroke. This means a dirty dot won't appear while a user is mid-edit until they press Done. A future improvement could update the dot in real-time during input events without a full re-render, e.g. by toggling a CSS class on the <td> directly."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:28:02Z",
          "note": "The mrHasChanges() comparison in config.js uses index-based positional matching (mrModels[i] vs mrOriginal[i]) rather than ID-based matching. This is correct for the current bulk-save pattern where array order is stable, but would produce false positives if array reordering were ever added. A future refactor could switch to ID-keyed comparison."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:28:02Z",
          "note": "The Add Model form's slug auto-derivation tracks 'previous value' via a custom property on the DOM input element (addNameInput._prevValue). This is a pragmatic workaround to avoid full re-renders on every keystroke, but it couples logic to DOM state. If the Add form were ever extracted into a component, this pattern would need to be replaced with explicit state tracking."
        }
      ]
    },
