        "All 9 acceptance criteria met. The implementation is frontend-only (config.js + styles.css) — no backend changes were needed. Key design decisions: bulk-save pattern (local state accumulates all edits until Save); dirty comparison against mrOriginal snapshot; strikethrough-then-Restore deletion UX; auto-slug derivation only fires when the slug hasn't been manually diverged from the auto-derived value. The mrRefreshDirtyDots() function is intentionally a no-op stub — dot updates are handled by full re-renders on explicit actions (Done, Cancel, Delete, Restore, Save). QA should verify: (1) tab state resets correctly on page reload; (2) unsaved-changes guard triggers when navigating away with pending edits; (3) 409 error message renders correctly (requires a model referenced by a persona assignment to be marked for deletion before saving)."
